                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Final Score: 35/100\r\n\r\nI'll say upfront that other reviews are correct that the puzzles themselves are compelling, and for a game that only sets you back $5, not bad; the hours you may sink in might make it worth it.\r\n\r\nThat said, it's impossible for me to say this game is really worth it, even for puzzle enthusiasts. Will you be challenged? Yes. Is there anything original or compelling about this title in its gameplay, visuals, or tech? No, none whatsoever. \r\n\r\nThis game suffers from considerable mediocrity and overly tedious movement mechanics in what could have been a top-down 2-D game without losing anything. Add to that bland production value and you've got a game that, had it released in the 90s, might have had something of a selling point, but with how many other, better, more polished options you have out there, it's just not worth your time or money.",
